  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 240,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your first wife is still named on your work \nretirement account. You are already telling  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6320,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yourself that doesn't matter because there is \na will and the will names the children. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will does not decide this one. The people who \npay that money out are required to follow the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18160,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paper they are holding. And the paper they are \nholding has her name on it. You did everything  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24240,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "asked of you at the bank. You requested the \nform. You wrote your children on it. That form  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30800,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is real and it works. It works on one account. \nIt does not reach the account where your shares  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37520,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are kept. It does not reach the small business \nyou run in your own name. It does not reach that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43040,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work retirement account. And it stops working on \nthe day the person you named dies before you do.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48960,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you never wrote a second name underneath four \naccounts, your children are named on none of them.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55600,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where each one stops and the words you \nuse this week to close it. Number one is the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "account where the person you named died before you \ndid. You wrote one name on that form. Your son,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67360,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your daughter, your husband, one name, and you \nnever went back because why would you? It was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73600,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "done. Then that person dies first. It happens more \nthan people allow themselves to think about. A son  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80160,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes at 61. A husband goes at 74. And on the day \nit happens, nobody at the bank telephones you to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say that your form has just stopped working \nbecause that is what happened to it. The form  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92400,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "names a person who is no longer alive. There is \nnobody left on it to receive anything. And a form  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98400,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a dead name on it protects nothing at all. \nSo the money goes where money goes when no living  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105040,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "name is attached. It goes to your estate, which is \nanother way of saying it goes to a court. and your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112400,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "family waits while a judge decides who gets what \nand when. That is the same court you filled the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118720,
    "dDurationMs": 8400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "form in to avoid. You did the work. You avoided \nnothing. The fix takes one line. When you fill  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127120,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that form in, you write a second name underneath \nthe first. The bank has a place for it. Most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133600,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people leave it blank because nobody points at it \nand nobody explains what it is for. That second  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140080,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "name does nothing at all while the first person \nis alive. It sits there. It costs you nothing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But on the day your first choice dies before \nyou, that second name steps in and the account  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152720,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still passes straight to a living person with no \ncourt, no waiting, no lawyer. And understand what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159840,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it means that this is the fix. The most common way \na beneficiary form fails is not that the form is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166800,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wrong. It is that the form was right on the day \nyou signed it and the world moved afterwards and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173600,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nobody is employed to tell you. Go and look at \nyour form. If there is one name on it, it is one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180000,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "death away from doing nothing. And think about who \nthat catches hardest. Somebody who did this early  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187120,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in their 60s while they were well and putting \ntheir affairs in order. They filled it in 20  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193520,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years ago and they have been carrying the comfort \nof it ever since. The person who never filled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199920,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the form in at all knows they have a problem. The \nperson who filled it in perfectly in 2006 does not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207920,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and will never be told. Number two is the account \nwhere your shares are kept. If you have money in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214880,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shares or funds, that money is not sitting in your \nbank. It is held at a different company, a broker,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222640,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it lives under a different set of rules \nentirely. The form you signed at your bank does  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228720,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not reach it. Not partly, not eventually. It has \nno effect there at all. Your bank cannot instruct  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236560,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that company. And that company has never seen your \nbank form. That account needs its own paperwork,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243120,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it is not even called the same thing. At a \nbank, it is payable on death. at a broker. It  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249440,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a transfer on death registration and you have \nto ask that company for it by that name. And this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255600,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "next fact is the reason this one catches so many \nfamilies. Whether that company offers it at all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261920,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is up to them. Some firms simply do not. There \nis no law forcing every broker to give you this.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268640,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if yours does not, then the only route your \nshares can take is through the court. Read that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274320,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again because it is unusual. On this one, doing \neverything right may still not be enough. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281200,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the only way to find out is to ask them directly. \nSo, put the question to them in these words. Do  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287840,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you offer transfer on death registration on this \naccount? And if you do, send me the form. If the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "answer is no, you have learned something today \nthat most people learn after they are gone. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have time to move that money somewhere that \ndoes offer it. And do not assume it is handled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because someone helped you set the account \nup years ago. The person who sold you those  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309920,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funds was paid to sell you those funds. Naming who \nreceives them was not part of that conversation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316720,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number three is the account for the small business \nyou run in your own name. A lot of people over 65  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323360,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have one. You cut lawns. You do books for two \nneighbors. You sell what you make. You opened  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an account so the money stayed separate from the \nhousehold. and the bank put the business name on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334800,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it. What that account actually is will surprise \nyou. If the business is just you with no company  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "registered behind it, then in the eyes of the \nlaw, that business does not exist as a separate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347440,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing. It has no life of its own. It is you with a \ndifferent name printed on the checks. Which means  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354000,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the money in it is your personal money. And when \nyou die, it does exactly what your personal money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359840,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does. It stops. It waits for the court and it \nis worse than an ordinary account for a reason  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366400,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that catches families offguard. Nobody can step in \nand keep the business running while they wait. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372880,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "invoices are not paid. The supplier is not paid. \nWhatever was owed to you stays owed and whatever  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379680,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you owed keeps growing and none of it can be \nsettled from an account nobody can reach. I have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385680,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heard from families who watched a small business \ndie in the 8 weeks after a funeral. Not because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the business was failing, but because the only \naccount it had was frozen and there was no name  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396720,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on it. So, if you have an account with a business \nname on it, go and ask one question. Can I add  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403600,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a beneficiary to this account? And if not, what \nwould let my family reach it? Some banks allow it,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410640,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some do not, and will tell you the account has to \nbe restructured first. Either answer is useful.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417120,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not asking is the only wrong move. Number four \nis the work retirement account with a name on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it from a marriage that ended. Check this one \ntonight. It holds more money than anything else  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most people leave behind. And its paperwork is \nthe oldest thing in the house. You filled that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434880,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "form in decades ago. You were married then. You \nwrote your wife on it because of course you did.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441680,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the marriage ended and you dealt with the \nhouse and the lawyers and the children and nobody  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447760,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in that room ever said the words retirement \naccount beneficiary form. Here is the rule and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454320,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is harder than people expect. Those plans are \nrequired to pay according to the plan documents  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460800,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they hold. Not your will, not the divorce papers, \nnot what everyone in the family knows you would  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467360,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have wanted, the form. So the money goes to a \nperson you have not spoken to in 20 years and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474480,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your children receive nothing from that account \nand there is nobody to be angry with because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480240,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every single person involved did exactly what they \nwere required to do. I want to be accurate with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you here because this one has moving parts. Some \nplans do cancel a former spouse automatically when  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493200,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a divorce comes through. Many do not. It depends \nentirely on the wording of the plan you are in,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499920,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means you cannot assume it either way. And \nthe only way to know is to ask. And if you married  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "again, your current wife has rights of her own \nin most workplace plans, which can change the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511680,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "answer completely. That is another reason to ask \nrather than guess. So telephone the plan and say  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519440,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this. I want to know who is currently named \nas beneficiary on my account and I want it in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526080,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "writing. Then if the name is wrong, ask for the \nform to change it and send it back the same week,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533680,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not the same month. There is no penalty for doing \nit today and no way to fix it afterwards. Number  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540960,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "five is not an account. It is a limit that changed \nand almost nobody has been told. You may have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heard that naming more people protects more of \nyour money. It used to work more generously than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553120,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it does now. That changed in the spring of 2024, \nand it changed for accounts that already existed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560480,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not just new ones. The rule, as it stands now, is \nthis money. An account with beneficiaries named on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566880,
    "dDurationMs": 8080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is protected up to $250,000 for each person you \nname, and it stops counting at five people. Five  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574960,
    "dDurationMs": 8800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "names, $1,250,000. And that is the ceiling for \nyou at that one bank. So if you name six children,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583760,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sixth name adds nothing. If you named eight \ngrandchildren, believing each one carried its own  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "protection, five of them do, and three of them \nare carrying nothing at all. And it applies to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595360,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accounts you opened years ago, and to money locked \nin a certificate, whatever the date on it says.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601440,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nobody wrote to tell existing customers that the \narithmetic under their account had changed. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607280,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rule simply started and the money above the \nline stopped being covered the same day. Now  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most people watching this are nowhere near \nthat ceiling. And I am not going to pretend  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618960,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "otherwise. But some of you sold a house. Some of \nyou have one bank holding everything because it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625360,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the bank you have used since 1970. If that \nis you, the money above that line is sitting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631680,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there with nothing behind it and moving part of \nit to a second bank fixes it in an afternoon.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637760,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the steps and one line before them. This is \ngeneral information about how these systems work,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not advice about your own situation. So read your \nown paperwork and ask your own bank and your own  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649840,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plan. This week, make four telephone calls and \nmake them in this order. Largest money first.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657040,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Call the work retirement plan. Ask who is named \nright now and ask for it in writing. That is the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "biggest amount and the oldest paperwork. So, \nit is where the worst surprise is likely to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be waiting. Call the company that holds your \nshares. Ask whether they offer transfer on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674080,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "death registration on your account. If they say \nyes, ask them to send the form. If they say no,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "write that down because you now have a \ndecision to make about where that money lives.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686240,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Go to your bank in person if you can and ask to \nsee the beneficiary form on every account you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692320,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hold there. Not one account, everyone. Then look \nfor the second line, the one under the first name,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and put a name in it. And if you have an account \nwith a business name on it, ask what can be done  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703840,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for that one because the answer is different at \ndifferent banks. Write down the date of every call  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710800,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the name of every person you speak to. You \nwill not remember in March which of these four  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716720,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you finished and the one you skip is the one that \ncosts. Now the warning and it belongs here because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723600,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are about to start telephoning about money and \ndeath and there are people who watch for exactly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729360,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that. Nobody from a bank or a retirement plan will \ntelephone you first about your beneficiaries. If a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736080,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "call comes in and the person on the line already \nseems to know who your children are, hang up.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742880,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ring the number printed on your own statement \ninstead. Nothing about this is urgent enough  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748720,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be settled with a stranger who called you. So \nthere they are one last time and every one of them  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755520,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a place where the form you already signed does \nnot reach. The account where the person you named  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761840,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "died before you did and there was no second name \nunderneath. The account where your shares are kept  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768000,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which needs its own paperwork and may not offer it \nat all. the account for the small business you run  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773840,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in your own name, which the law does not treat as \nseparate from you, and the work retirement account  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still holding a name from a marriage that ended, \nwhere the plan is required to follow the paper and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784800,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not your will. None of this is hidden, and none \nof it is unfair. Every rule here is written down,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and every one of them was followed. The whole \nthing works this way because filling in a form  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once was treated as the end of the job and \nnobody was ever given the task of telling you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800800,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when it stopped working. Go and look at your forms \ntonight. And if your mother or your father filled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one in 20 years ago and has never looked at it \nsince, telephone them and ask them one question."
    } ]
  } ]
}
